{
  "code": "LING-PHD",
  "reviewed": "2026-10-23",
  "summary": "The nine basic courses follow the Bulletin's sets: either two Group I sets and one Group II set plus one more Group II course, or the reverse, then one Group III methods course and one more course from any group. All nine, and LINGUIST 200, must be letter graded with a B or better and taken for at least 2 units. The audit also checks the first-year courses (LINGUIST 294, 395, 396, 398) and LINGUIST 394. Your advisor and the department check by hand the 3.3 GPA, the qualifying papers, teaching, the research quarter, candidacy, the language requirement, the oral exam and the dissertation. The extra course in (d) must come from a set you did not use. Left: the audit does not stop the course in (f) from repeating a set you already used, and the Cognitive Science subplan has no listed requirements (see the Student Services Officer).",
